      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:120mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2023-june/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. A ball is projected from O on horizontal ground at speed 28 m s^-1 at angle alpha above the ground and follows a parabolic path; it passes through A, which is 40 m horizontally and 20 m vertically from O, on the way down.\"></figure><p>A small ball is projected with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"28\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> from a point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> on horizontal ground.</p><p>After moving for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> seconds, the ball passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> horizontally and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> vertically from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, as shown in Figure 2.</p><p>The motion of the ball from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is modelled as that of a particle moving freely under gravity.</p><p>Given that the ball is projected at an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> to the ground, use the model to</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\dfrac{10}{7\\cos\\alpha}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan^2\\alpha-4\\tan\\alpha+3=0\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>find the greatest possible height, in metres, of the ball above the ground as the ball moves from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The model does not include air resistance.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>State one other limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
